{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_0136aPeKiyeU3b23CaDXxbF2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Wait, I just realized there's an issue with my App.tsx. I'm using a `<Route element={...}>` wrapper but it's using AppLayout as the wrapper with children, but React Router uses `<Outlet>` for nested routes, not children. Let me fix this.\n\nIn React Router v6, when you have a parent route with an element and child routes, the parent element needs to use `<Outlet />` to render the child. But AppLayout currently uses `children` prop pattern.\n\nI need to either:\n1. Update AppLayout to also use `<Outlet />` for nested route children, OR\n\n\n2. Wrap each page directly in AppLayout, or create a layout route pattern where the layout uses `<Outlet />`.\n\nThe cleaner approach for React Router v6 is to have the layout route use `<Outlet>`. I could create a LayoutRoute component that renders AppLayout with Outlet inside, or just wrap each page directly in AppLayout. Let me go with the LayoutRoute component approach since it's cleaner and avoids repetition.\n\nI'll create an AppLayoutRoute component that wraps the Outlet with AppLayout, then use it as a parent route for all the pages. This way I can nest the routes under it and keep the layout consistent across all pages. Let me update App.tsx with this pattern.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1519,"cache_read_input_tokens":30294,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1519},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"572f6923-00ff-4cf3-9331-5f53f98a9735","uuid":"5d1bf5ad-8b27-4f2c-b769-0faf9634832d"}
