*\n      * TODO: Real API binding\n      * import { apiService } from '@/lib/api';\n      * const response = await apiService.get({ endpoint: '/xyz/list', params: { page, limit, ...filters } });\n      * setData(response.data);\n      */\n\n     Then use mock data below the commented block. Leave the commented block in place — a future pass will uncomment it and delete the mock.\n\n5. FORM FIELDS FROM request_payload_ui_passing (map each description to the correct UI):\n   - \"From an input field with email regex validation\" → <Input type=\"email\"> with regex validation\n   - \"From a text input field ... required validation\" → <Input> required\n   - \"From a textarea field\" → <Textarea>\n   - \"From a number input ...\" → <Input type=\"number\">\n   - \"From a date picker returning ISO 8601 string\" → date input returning YYYY-MM-DD\n   - \"From a dropdown with hardcoded enum options: [...]\" → <Select> with those exact options (static, fine for small enums)\n   - \"From a SEARCHABLE dropdown (Combobox) populated by GET /abc/list ...\" → shadcn Combobox (Popover + Command + CommandInput + CommandList + CommandItem). Initial render shows first 10 mock records. As user types, a 300ms-debounced handler filters the mock list by the search term (in the mock data pass) and shows the filtered results. Add the commented real-API block showing the real GET call with { page: 1, limit: 10, search: searchTerm } params. Use cmdk-compatible Combobox — NEVER a static <Select> that renders all records at once.\n   - \"From a dropdown populated by GET /abc/list ...\" (without SEARCHABLE keyword) → treat as searchable anyway per the rule above; do not render a static <Select> for lookup data\n   - \"From a SEARCHABLE multi-select chip input populated by GET /abc/list ...\" → shadcn Combobox in multi-select mode with chip display; same initial-10 + debounced-search pattern, sends array of ids\n   - \"From a toggle switch\" → <Switch> or <Checkbox>\n   - \"From a file input ...\" → <Input type=\"file\">\n   - \"From pagination control ...\" → pagination component\n   - \"From a filter dropdown ...\" → filter <Select> (static enum filters are fine; lookup-based filters use the same searchable Combobox pattern)\n   - \"Injected from the current route params ...\" → read from useParams(), not a user input\n   - \"Injected from the authenticated user session ...\" → read from MockAuthContext, not a user input\n\n5.5. SEARCHABLE LOOKUP DROPDOWN — MANDATORY PATTERN for any field populated by GET /{entity}/list:\n   - NEVER render a lookup dropdown as a static <Select> that maps over all mock records at once.\n   - Use shadcn Combobox (Popover + Command components from @/components/ui/command). The component must:\n     a) Show the first 10 mock records on mount (slice(0, 10))\n     b) Include a search input at the top (CommandInput)\n     c) Filter the mock records by the search term via useState + useMemo (for mock mode) — this simulates the real server-side search\n     d) Display a \"No results found\" empty state when filtered list is empty\n     e) On select, store the picked entity's id in form state\n   - Include a commented real-API block above the filter logic showing the real call:\n     /*\n      * TODO: Real API binding (searchable lookup)\n      * const [searchTerm, setSearchTerm] = useState('');\n      * const debouncedSearch = useDebounce(searchTerm, 300);\n      * useEffect(() => {\n      *   apiService.get({ endpoint: '/abc/list', params: { page: 1, limit: 10, search: debouncedSearch } })\n      *     .then(res => setOptions(res.data));\n      * }, [debouncedSearch]);\n      */\n   - The mock pass keeps a larger mock array (e.g. 30-50 entries for lookup entities) so the searchable behavior can be demonstrated during development even before the real API is wired.\n\n5.6. HARDCODED OPTION ARRAYS:\n   - When generating hardcoded arrays for dropdowns, filters, or status/priority/role/category options (e.g., const STATUS_OPTIONS = [...], const ROLES = [...]),\n     ALWAYS add a comment above: // TODO: fetch from backend config API when available\n   - This marks them for future replacement. Applies to ANY array of options that represents domain configuration: statuses, priorities, roles, categories, types, visibility levels, frequencies, etc.\n   - Do NOT add this comment to pure UI constants (color maps, icon maps, column definitions, route configs, pagination sizes).\n\n5.7. FILE INPUT HANDLING:\n   - When a form has a file input (avatar, image, document, attachment):\n     - Store the File object in state via onChange\n     - Before submitting to the API, convert File to base64 string:\n       const toBase64 = (file: File): Promise<string> => new Promise((resolve) => {\n         const reader = new FileReader();\n         reader.onloadend = () => resolve(reader.result as string);\n         reader.readAsDataURL(file);\n       });\n     - Send the base64 string in the API payload, NOT the raw File object\n     - Include this conversion in BOTH the commented TODO block and the mock handler\n\n6. EVERY FIELD in request_payload must have a corresponding input in the UI. If request_payload has 7 fields, the form has 7 inputs (unless a field is marked as route-param or session-injected).\n\n7. FORMS LIVE INSIDE MODALS:\n   - Create/edit forms MUST be inside a <Dialog> or <Sheet>, opened by a button click\n   - Never render a form statically on the page\n\n7.5. TABLE ROW ACTIONS MUST BE IN A KEBAB MENU (3-dot dropdown):\n   - Any data table with row-level actions (Edit, Delete, Remove, Archive, Duplicate, View, Approve, Reject, Assign, etc.) MUST group ALL row actions under a single kebab-menu trigger (3 vertical dots icon) at the end of each row.\n   - Use shadcn <DropdownMenu> + <DropdownMenuTrigger> + <DropdownMenuContent> + <DropdownMenuItem> for this, with a <Button variant=\"ghost\" size=\"icon\"> containing a <MoreVertical /> (or <MoreHorizontal />) icon from lucide-react as the trigger.\n   - Destructive items (Delete, Remove, Archive) must use a distinct visual treatment — typically wrap inside <DropdownMenuSeparator> + red text (className=\"text-destructive focus:text-destructive\").\n   - Never render multiple individual action buttons directly in the Actions column. A table with `<Button>Edit</Button> <Button>Remove</Button>` side-by-side in every row is WRONG — they must collapse into a single `<MoreVertical />` trigger.\n   - Example shape for the Actions column cell:\n     ```tsx\n     <TableCell className=\"text-right\">\n       <DropdownMenu>\n         <DropdownMenuTrigger asChild>\n           <Button variant=\"ghost\" size=\"icon\">\n             <MoreVertical className=\"h-4 w-4\" />\n           </Button>\n         </DropdownMenuTrigger>\n         <DropdownMenuContent align=\"end\">\n           <DropdownMenuItem onClick={() => handleEdit(row)}>Edit</DropdownMenuItem>\n           <DropdownMenuSeparator />\n           <DropdownMenuItem className=\"text-destructive focus:text-destructive\" onClick={() => handleDelete(row)}>Delete</DropdownMenuItem>\n         </DropdownMenuContent>\n       </DropdownMenu>\n     </TableCell>\n     ```\n   - Only exception: a SINGLE primary action per row (e.g. just \"View\") can stay as an inline button since there's nothing to group. The moment there are 2+ actions, they collapse into the kebab menu.\n   - Bulk-action buttons that act on selected rows (not row-level) stay above the table as regular buttons — this rule only applies to per-row actions inside the Actions column.\n\n8. DO NOT:\n   - Wrap the page in <AppLayout> or any layout shell — the router already wraps pages\n   - Import a real auth context — use MockAuthContext if needed\n   - Create pages for any page_id other than yours (page_3_sub_2)\n   - Modify /planner/ files\n   - Modify shared layout/router files\n\n9. DO:\n   - Follow the description faithfully\n   - Use shadcn/ui components\n   - Show loading states are OK but should be brief since mock data is instant\n   - Use toast for user feedback on actions\n   - Keep every commented real-API block visible and clearly labeled\n\nSHARED CONTEXT:\n- ThemeContext: const { themeMode, setThemeMode } = useTheme(); import { useTheme } from '@/contexts/ThemeContext';\n- Toast: import { toast } from '@/lib/toast'; toast.success('msg'); toast.error('msg');\n- formatCurrency: import { formatCurrency } from '@/lib/formatCurrency';\n- AppLayout is applied at the router level — pages return ONLY their content, they MUST NOT wrap themselves in <AppLayout>\n- shadcn/ui components are available at @/components/ui/*\n- Mock auth state (if present) comes from MockAuthContext","outputFile":"/tmp/claude-1001/-home-ubuntu-code-project-code-code-base-app-7a97b333c52f0a2e89b9d85da46ab74b/6cbff16b-eda9-4a5c-9560-4577d39c4a2c/tasks/a17ed00ba41ef5b01.output","canReadOutputFile":true}}
