d + CommandInput + CommandList + CommandItem). Initial render shows first 10 mock records. As user types, a 300ms-debounced handler filters the mock list by the search term (in the mock data pass) and shows the filtered results. Add the commented real-API block showing the real GET call with { page: 1, limit: 10, search: searchTerm } params. Use cmdk-compatible Combobox — NEVER a static <Select> that renders all records at once.\n   - \"From a dropdown populated by GET /abc/list ...\" (without SEARCHABLE keyword) → treat as searchable anyway per the rule above; do not render a static <Select> for lookup data\n   - \"From a SEARCHABLE multi-select chip input populated by GET /abc/list ...\" → shadcn Combobox in multi-select mode with chip display; same initial-10 + debounced-search pattern, sends array of ids\n   - \"From a toggle switch\" → <Switch> or <Checkbox>\n   - \"From a file input ...\" → <Input type=\"file\">\n   - \"From pagination control ...\" → pagination component\n   - \"From a filter dropdown ...\" → filter <Select> (static enum filters are fine; lookup-based filters use the same searchable Combobox pattern)\n   - \"Injected from the current route params ...\" → read from useParams(), not a user input\n   - \"Injected from the authenticated user session ...\" → read from MockAuthContext, not a user input\n\n5.5. SEARCHABLE LOOKUP DROPDOWN — MANDATORY PATTERN for any field populated by GET /{entity}/list:\n   - NEVER render a lookup dropdown as a static <Select> that maps over all mock records at once.\n   - Use shadcn Combobox (Popover + Command components from @/components/ui/command). The component must:\n     a) Show the first 10 mock records on mount (slice(0, 10))\n     b) Include a search input at the top (CommandInput)\n     c) Filter the mock records by the search term via useState + useMemo (for mock mode) — this simulates the real server-side search\n     d) Display a \"No results found\" empty state when filtered list is empty\n     e) On select, store the picked entity's id in form state\n   - Include a commented real-API block above the filter logic showing the real call:\n     /*\n      * TODO: Real API binding (searchable lookup)\n      * const [searchTerm, setSearchTerm] = useState('');\n      * const debouncedSearch = useDebounce(searchTerm, 300);\n      * useEffect(() => {\n      *   apiService.get({ endpoint: '/abc/list', params: { page: 1, limit: 10, search: debouncedSearch } })\n      *     .then(res => setOptions(res.data));\n      * }, [debouncedSearch]);\n      */\n   - The mock pass keeps a larger mock array (e.g. 30-50 entries for lookup entities) so the searchable behavior can be demonstrated during development even before the real API is wired.\n\n5.6. HARDCODED OPTION ARRAYS:\n   - When generating hardcoded arrays for dropdowns, filters, or status/priority/role/category options (e.g., const STATUS_OPTIONS = [...], const ROLES = [...]),\n     ALWAYS add a comment above: // TODO: fetch from backend config API when available\n   - This marks them for future replacement. Applies to ANY array of options that represents domain configuration: statuses, priorities, roles, categories, types, visibility levels, frequencies, etc.\n   - Do NOT add this comment to pure UI constants (color maps, icon maps, column definitions, route configs, pagination sizes).\n\n5.7. FILE INPUT HANDLING:\n   - When a form has a file input (avatar, image, document, attachment):\n     - Store the File object in state via onChange\n     - Before submitting to the API, convert File to base64 string:\n       const toBase64 = (file: File): Promise<string> => new Promise((resolve) => {\n         const reader = new FileReader();\n         reader.onloadend = () => resolve(reader.result as string);\n         reader.readAsDataURL(file);\n       });\n     - Send the base64 string in the API payload, NOT the raw File object\n     - Include this conversion in BOTH the commented TODO block and the mock handler\n\n6. EVERY FIELD