le\">\n   - \"From pagination control ...\" → pagination component\n   - \"From a filter dropdown ...\" → filter <Select> (static enum filters are fine; lookup-based filters use the same searchable Combobox pattern)\n   - \"Injected from the current route params ...\" → read from useParams(), not a user input\n   - \"Injected from the authenticated user session ...\" → read from MockAuthContext, not a user input\n\n5.5. SEARCHABLE LOOKUP DROPDOWN — MANDATORY PATTERN for any field populated by GET /{entity}/list:\n   - NEVER render a lookup dropdown as a static <Select> that maps over all mock records at once.\n   - Use shadcn Combobox (Popover + Command components from @/components/ui/command). The component must:\n     a) Show the first 10 mock records on mount (slice(0, 10))\n     b) Include a search input at the top (CommandInput)\n     c) Filter the mock records by the search term via useState + useMemo (for mock mode) — this simulates the real server-side search\n     d) Display a \"No results found\" empty state when filtered list is empty\n     e) On select, store the picked entity's id in form state\n   - Include a commented real-API block above the filter logic showing the real call:\n     /*\n      * TODO: Real API binding (searchable lookup)\n      * const [searchTerm, setSearchTerm] = useState('');\n      * const debouncedSearch = useDebounce(searchTerm, 300);\n      * useEffect(() => {\n      *   apiService.get({ endpoint: '/abc/list', params: { page: 1, limit: 10, search: debouncedSearch } })\n      *     .then(res => setOptions(res.data));\n      * }, [debouncedSearch]);\n      */\n   - The mock pass keeps a larger mock array (e.g. 30-50 entries for lookup entities) so the searchable behavior can be demonstrated during development even before the real API is wired.\n\n5.6. HARDCODED OPTION ARRAYS:\n   - When generating hardcoded arrays for dropdowns, filters, or status/priority/role/category options (e.g., const STATUS_OPTIONS = [...], const ROLES = [