: 'Engineered a high-strength industrial wastewater system handling 2,400 m³/day with high BOD/COD loads, achieving effluent standards for discharge to municipal sewer.',\n    location: 'Watou, Belgium',\n    year: '2023',\n    thumbnail_url: 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1574944985070-8f3ebc6b79d2?w=600&h=400&fit=crop',\n    created_at: '2023-06-15T14:30:00Z',\n  },\n  {\n    id: 'proj-014',\n    title: 'Smart Irrigation Scheduling for Golf Courses',\n    client: 'PGA Tour Golf Courses Holdings',\n    sector: 'Agriculture',\n    project_type: 'Irrigation',\n    challenge_summary: 'Deployed soil moisture sensor networks and evapotranspiration-based scheduling algorithms to reduce irrigation water use by 42% across 12 championship courses.',\n    location: 'Orlando, Florida, USA',\n    year: '2024',\n    thumbnail_url: 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1594950195005-bd02d8146fa4?w=600&h=400&fit=crop',\n    created_at: '2024-03-08T11:15:00Z',\n  },\n  {\n    id: 'proj-015',\n    title: 'Groundwater Contamination Remediation Design',\n    client: 'US Army Corps of Engineers',\n    sector: 'Government',\n    project_type: 'Environmental Consulting',\n    challenge_summary: 'Designed an enhanced bioremediation system for a former industrial site, achieving 94% reduction in trichloroethylene concentrations within 18 months.',\n    location: 'Camp Lejeune, North Carolina, USA',\n    year: '2023',\n    thumbnail_url: 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1552084117-56a987666889?w=600&h=400&fit=crop',\n    created_at: '2023-12-01T08:45:00Z',\n  },\n  {\n    id: 'proj-016',\n    title: 'Largest Urban Water Loss Reduction Program',\n    client: 'Jakarta Provincial Water Utility (PDAM)',\n    sector: 'Urban Infrastructure',\n    project_type: 'Hydraulic Modeling',\n    challenge_summary: 'Led a systematic NRW reduction program using pressure management, active leak detection, and meter replacement, saving 180 MLD across 2.4 million connections.',\n    location: 'Jakarta, Indonesia',\n    year: '2024',\n    thumbnail_url: 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1558618666-fcd25c85cd64?w=600&h=400&fit=crop',\n    created_at: '2024-04-10T10:30:00Z',\n  },\n  {\n    id: 'proj-017',\n    title: 'Packaged Water Treatment Plant for Mining Camp',\n    client: 'BHP Billiton',\n    sector: 'Industrial',\n    project_type: 'WTP Design',\n    challenge_summary: 'Designed a compact 1.2 MLD packaged WTP with iron/manganese removal and UV disinfection for a remote mining operation, delivered on a 16-week fast-track schedule.',\n    location: 'Pilbara Region, Western Australia',\n    year: '2023',\n    thumbnail_url: 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1574952564156-5f5e4d194a18?w=600&h=400&fit=crop',\n    created_at: '2023-08-05T13:00:00Z',\n  },\n  {\n    id: 'proj-018',\n    title: 'Transboundary Aquifer Assessment',\n    client: 'International Boundary and Water Commission',\n    sector: 'Government',\n    project_type: 'Environmental Consulting',\n    challenge_summary: 'Conducted joint hydrological assessment of the Hueco Bolson aquifer spanning US-Mexico border, developing shared management protocols for sustainable extraction.',\n    location: 'El Paso, Texas / Ciudad Juárez, Chihuahua',\n    year: '2023',\n    thumbnail_url: 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1449034446853-66c86144b0ad?w=600&h=400&fit=crop',\n    created_at: '2023-04-20T09:30:00Z',\n  },\n  {\n    id: 'proj-019',\n    title: 'Sewer Network Asset Management GIS Platform',\n    client: 'London Borough of Lambeth',\n    sector: 'Urban Infrastructure',\n    project_type: 'GIS Integration',\n    challenge_summary: 'Built an enterprise GIS platform integrating CCTV inspection data, asset condition scores, and failure prediction models to optimize $45M annual capital renewal budget.',\n    location: 'London, United Kingdom',\n    year: '2024',\n    thumbnail_url: 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1513635269975-59663e0ac1ad?w=600&h=400&fit=crop',\n    created_at: '2024-01-15T15:00:00Z',\n  },\n  {\n    id: 'proj-020',\n    title: 'Rice Farm Subsurface Drip Irrigation',\n    client: 'Syserco Agricultural Development',\n    sector: 'Agriculture',\n    project_type: 'Irrigation',\n    challenge_summary: 'Designed and commissioned SDI systems for 3,200 hectares of rice cultivation in the Sacramento Valley, achieving 55% water savings versus conventional flood irrigation.',\n    location: 'Willows, California, USA',\n    year: '2023',\n    thumbnail_url: 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1500382017468-9049fed747ef?w=600&h=400&fit=crop',\n    created_at: '2023-07-28T12:15:00Z',\n  },\n  {\n    id: 'proj-021',\n    title: 'Water Treatment Plant Residuals Management',\n    client: 'New York City Department of Environmental Protection',\n    sector: 'Government',\n    project_type: 'WTP Design',\n    challenge_summary: 'Designed thickened sludge handling and filter press dewatering facilities for three major WTPs, reducing residuals volume by 70% and lowering disposal costs.',\n    location: 'New York City, New York, USA',\n    year: '2024',\n    thumbnail_url: 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?w=600&h=400&fit=crop',\n    created_at: '2024-02-05T14:00:00Z',\n  },\n  {\n    id: 'proj-022',\n    title: 'HVAC Condensate Recovery Hydraulic Analysis',\n    client: 'Google Data Centers',\n    sector: 'Industrial',\n    project_type: 'Hydraulic Modeling',\n    challenge_summary: 'Performed hydraulic analysis of rooftop condensate recovery systems across 12 data center facilities, enabling 18 MLD of recovered water for cooling tower makeup.',\n    location: 'The Dalles, Oregon, USA',\n    year: '2023',\n    thumbnail_url: 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1451187580459-43490279c0fa?w=600&h=400&fit=crop',\n    created_at: '2023-11-08T10:45:00Z',\n  },\n  {\n    id: 'proj-023',\n    title: 'Constructed Wetland for Secondary Effluent Polishing',\n    client: 'Town of Queen Creek',\n    sector: 'Government',\n    project_type: 'Environmental Consulting',\n    challenge_summary: 'Designed a 12-hectare surface flow constructed wetland providing tertiary treatment for treated wastewater, creating wildlife habitat and public recreation space.',\n    location: 'Queen Creek, Arizona, USA',\n    year: '2024',\n    thumbnail_url: 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1441974231531-c6227db76b6e?w=600&h=400&fit=crop',\n    created_at: '2024-03-22T09:00:00Z',\n  },\n  {\n    id: 'proj-024',\n    title: 'Regional Drainage Master Plan',\n    client: 'Ontario Ministry of Infrastructure',\n    sector: 'Government',\n    project_type: 'Hydraulic Modeling',\n    challenge_summary: 'Developed a 50-year drainage master plan using coupled 1D/2D models to evaluate climate change impacts and prioritize $3.8B in infrastructure investments.',\n    location: 'Greater Toronto Area, Ontario, Canada',\n    year: '2023',\n    thumbnail_url: 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1518167628171-60c5ef9b4a3c?w=600&h=400&fit=crop',\n    created_at: '2023-09-14T11:30:00Z',\n  },\n  {\n    id: 'proj-025',\n    title: 'Brackish Groundwater Desalination for Agriculture',\n    client: 'Imperial Irrigation District',\n    sector: 'Agriculture',\n    project_type: 'WTP Design',\n    challenge_summary: 'Designed a 3 MLD brackish groundwater RO system providing drought-resilient irrigation water supply, featuring boron-selective membranes for crop safety.',\n    location: 'Imperial Valley, California, USA',\n    year: '2024',\n    thumbnail_url: 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1500382017468-9049fed747ef?w=600&h=400&fit=crop',\n    created_at: '2024-04-05T08:00:00Z',\n  },\n  {\n    id: 'proj-026',\n    title: 'Combined Sewer Overflow Long-Term Control Plan',\n    client: 'DC Water',\n    sector: 'Urban Infrastructure',\n    project_type: 'STP Design',\n    challenge_summary: 'Developed a 25-year LTCP using real-time control sensors and storage tunnels to reduce CSO events by 94%, meeting EPA consent decree requirements.',\n    location: 'Washington, D.C., USA',\n    year: '2023',\n    thumbnail_url: 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1559839734-2b71ea197ec2?w=600&h=400&fit=crop',\n    created_at: '2023-06-22T14:30:00Z',\n  },\n  {\n    id: 'proj-027',\n    title: 'Mobile Water Treatment Unit for Emergency Response',\n    client: 'International Red Cross / Red Crescent',\n    sector: 'Government',\n    project_type: 'WTP Design',\n    challenge_summary: 'Engineered a containerized 500 m³/day mobile WTP with rapid deployment capability for emergency water supply in disaster-affected regions.',\n    location: 'Geneva, Switzerland (Global Deployment)',\n    year: '2024',\n    thumbnail_url: 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1552084117-56a987666889?w=600&h=400&fit=crop',\n    created_at: '2024-01-30T10:00:00Z',\n  },\n  {\n    id: 'proj-028',\n    title: 'Vineyard Micro-Irrigation System Upgrade',\n    client: 'Robert Mondavi Winery',\n    sector: 'Agriculture',\n    project_type: 'Irrigation',\n    challenge_summary: 'Retrofit 800 acres of premium vineyard blocks with pressure-compensating drippers and wireless soil moisture monitoring, improving yield uniformity by 35%.',\n    location: 'Napa Valley, California, USA',\n    year: '2023',\n    thumbnail_url: 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1474722883778-792e7990302f?w=600&h=400&fit=crop',\n    created_at: '2023-05-12T13:45:00Z',\n  },\n  {\n    id: 'proj-029',\n    title: 'Water Utility SCADA-EMS Integration',\n    client: 'Bay Area Water Supply & Conservation Agency',\n    sector: 'Urban Infrastructure',\n    project_type: 'GIS Integration',\n    challenge_summary: 'Integrated 14 SCADA systems with an enterprise GIS and energy management platform, enabling real-time optimization of pump schedules across 8 member agencies.',\n    location: 'San Francisco Bay Area, California, USA',\n    year: '2024',\n    thumbnail_url: 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1451187580459-43490279c0fa?w=600&h=400&fit=crop',\n    created_at: '2024-03-01T11:00:00Z',\n  },\n  {\n    id: 'proj-030',\n    title: 'Aquifer Storage and Recovery Feasibility Study',\n    client: 'Orange County Water District',\n    sector: 'Government',\n    project_type: 'Environmental Consulting',\n    challenge_summary: 'Conducted field-scale ASR feasibility assessment including water quality compatibility testing, recovered water credit accounting, and monitoring well network design.',\n    location: 'Orange County, California, USA',\n    year: '2023',\n    thumbnail_url: 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?w=600&h=400&fit=crop',\n    created_at: '2023-10-25T09:30:00Z',\n  },\n];\n\n// ── Helper to fetch paginated/filtered projects ───────────────────────────────\n\ninterface FetchProjectsParams {\n  page: number;\n  limit: number;\n  sector: string;\n  projectType: string;\n}\n\ninterface FetchProjectsResult {\n  message: string;\n  data: Project[];\n  total: number;\n  page: number;\n  limit: number;\n  totalPages: number;\n}\n\n/**\n * Fetches paginated and filtered project list (mock implementation).\n * In production, replace with:\n *\n * TODO: Real API binding\n * import { apiService } from '@/lib/api';\n * const response = await apiService.get({\n *   endpoint: '/projects/list',\n *   params: { page, limit, sector, project_type: projectType },\n * });\n * return response.data;\n */\nconst fetchProjects = async (params: FetchProjectsParams): Promise<FetchProjectsResult> => {\n  // Simulate network delay\n  await new Promise((resolve) => setTimeout(resolve, 300));\n\n  const { page, limit, sector, projectType } = params;\n\n  let filtered = MOCK_PROJECTS;\n\n  // Apply sector filter\n  if (sector) {\n    filtered = filtered.filter((p) => p.sector === sector);\n  }\n\n  // Apply project type filter\n  if (projectType) {\n    filtered = filtered.filter((p) => p.project_type === projectType);\n  }\n\n  const total = filtered.length;\n  const totalPages = Math.ceil(total / limit);\n  const startIndex = (page - 1) * limit;\n  const paginatedData = filtered.slice(startIndex, startIndex + limit);\n\n  return {\n    message: 'Projects retrieved successfully',\n    data: paginatedData,\n    total,\n    page,\n    limit,\n    totalPages,\n  };\n};\n\n// ── Projects Page ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nconst Projects = () => {\n  const navigate = useNavigate();\n\n  // Filter/sort state\n  const [page, setPage] = useState(1);\n  const [sector, setSector] = useState('');\n  const [projectType, setProjectType] = useState('');\n\n  // Data state\n  const [projectsData, setProjectsData] = useState<FetchProjectsResult | null>(null);\n  const [isLoading, setIsLoading] = useState(true);\n\n  // Fetch projects when filters or page change\n  useMemo(() => {\n    setIsLoading(true);\n    fetchProjects({ page, limit: PAGE_SIZE, sector, projectType })\n      .then((result) => {\n        setProjectsData(result);\n        setIsLoading(false);\n      })\n      .catch(() => {\n        toast.error('Failed to load projects');\n        setIsLoading(false);\n      });\n  }, [page, sector, projectType]);\n\n  // Reset to page 1 when filter changes\n  const handleSectorChange = (value: string) => {\n    setSector(value);\n    setPage(1);\n  };\n\n  const handleProjectTypeChange = (value: string) => {\n    setProjectType(value);\n    setPage(1);\n  };\n\n  const handleClearFilters = () => {\n    setSector('');\n    setProjectType('');\n    setPage(1);\n  };\n\n  const hasActiveFilters = sector || projectType;\n\n  // Generate pagination items\n  const getPaginationItems = () => {\n    if (!projectsData) return [];\n    const { totalPages } = projectsData;\n    const items: (number | 'ellipsis' | 'previous' | 'next')[] = [];\n\n    if (totalPages <= 7) {\n      for (let i = 1; i <= totalPages; i++) items.push(i);\n    } else {\n      items.push(1);\n      if (page > 3) items.push('ellipsis');\n      for (let i = Math.max(2, page - 1); i <= Math.min(totalPages - 1, page + 1); i++) {\n        items.push(i);\n      }\n      if (page < totalPages - 2) items.push('ellipsis');\n      items.push(totalPages);\n    }\n\n    return items;\n  };\n\n  return (\n    <div className=\"min-h-screen\">\n      {/* ── Page Header ────────────────────────────────────────────────── */}\n      <section className=\"bg-muted/30 py-16 md:py-24\">\n        <div className=\"container mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8\">\n          <div className=\"text-center max-w-3xl mx-auto\">\n            <h1 className=\"text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold tracking-tight mb-4\">\n              Our Projects\n            </h1>\n            <p className=\"text-lg text-muted-foreground\">\n              Explore Hydrologic Innovation's portfolio of completed and ongoing engineering\n              projects. Each case study demonstrates our expertise in solving complex water\n              infrastructure challenges across diverse sectors.\n            </p>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      {/* ── Filters ───────────────────────────────────────────────────── */}\n      <section className=\"border-b bg-card/50\">\n        <div className=\"container mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-4\">\n          <div className=\"flex flex-wrap items-center gap-4\">\n            {/* Sector Filter */}\n            <div className=\"flex items-center gap-2\">\n              <span className=\"text-sm font-medium text-muted-foreground\">Sector:</span>\n              <Select value={sector} onValueChange={handleSectorChange}>\n                <SelectTrigger className=\"w-[200px]\">\n                  <SelectValue placeholder=\"All Sectors\" />\n                </SelectTrigger>\n                <SelectContent>\n                  {SECTOR_OPTIONS.map((opt) => (\n                    <SelectItem key={opt.value} value={opt.value}>\n                      {opt.label}\n                    </SelectItem>\n                  ))}\n                </SelectContent>\n              </Select>\n            </div>\n\n            {/* Project Type Filter */}\n            <div className=\"flex items-center gap-2\">\n              <span className=\"text-sm font-medium text-muted-foreground\">Type:</span>\n              <Select value={projectType} onValueChange={handleProjectTypeChange}>\n                <SelectTrigger className=\"w-[220px]\">\n                  <SelectValue placeholder=\"All Project Types\" />\n                </SelectTrigger>\n                <SelectContent>\n                  {PROJECT_TYPE_OPTIONS.map((opt) => (\n                    <SelectItem key={opt.value} value={opt.value}>\n                      {opt.label}\n                    </SelectItem>\n                  ))}\n                </SelectContent>\n              </Select>\n            </div>\n\n            {/* Clear Filters */}\n            {hasActiveFilters && (\n              <Button\n                variant=\"ghost\"\n                size=\"sm\"\n                onClick={handleClearFilters}\n                className=\"text-muted-foreground hover:text-foreground\"\n              >\n                <X className=\"h-4 w-4 mr-1\" />\n                Clear filters\n              </Button>\n            )}\n\n            {/* Results count */}\n            {projectsData && (\n              <div className=\"ml-auto text-sm text-muted-foreground\">\n                {projectsData.total} project{projectsData.total !== 1 ? 's' : ''} found\n              </div>\n            )}\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      {/* ── Projects Grid ───────────────────────────────────────────────── */}\n      <section className=\"py-12 md:py-16\">\n        <div className=\"container mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8\">\n          {isLoading ? (\n            // Loading skeleton\n            <div className=\"grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3\">\n              {Array.from({ length: PAGE_SIZE }).map((_, i) => (\n                <Card key={i} className=\"overflow-hidden\">\n                  <div className=\"h-48 bg-muted animate-pulse\" />\n                  <CardHeader>\n                    <div className=\"h-6 bg-muted animate-pulse rounded w-3/4 mb-2\" />\n                    <div className=\"h-4 bg-muted animate-pulse rounded w-1/2\" />\n                  </CardHeader>\n                  <CardContent>\n                    <div className=\"h-4 bg-muted animate-pulse rounded w-full mb-2\" />\n                    <div className=\"h-4 bg-muted animate-pulse rounded w-2/3\" />\n                  </CardContent>\n                </Card>\n              ))}\n            </div>\n          ) : projectsData?.data.length === 0 ? (\n            // Empty state\n            <div className=\"text-center py-16\">\n              <Filter className=\"h-12 w-12 text-muted-foreground mx-auto mb-4\" />\n              <h3 className=\"text-lg font-semibold mb-2\">No projects found</h3>\n              <p className=\"text-muted-foreground mb-4\">\n                Try adjusting your filters to see more results.\n              </p>\n              {hasActiveFilters && (\n                <Button variant=\"outline\" onClick={handleClearFilters}>\n                  Clear all filters\n                </Button>\n              )}\n            </div>\n          ) : (\n            // Project cards grid\n            <div className=\"grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3\">\n              {projectsData?.data.map((project) => (\n                <Card\n                  key={project.id}\n                  className=\"group cursor-pointer overflow-hidden hover:shadow-lg transition-all duration-300 hover:-translate-y-1\"\n                  onClick={() => navigate(`/projects/${project.id}`)}\n                >\n                  {/* Thumbnail */}\n                  <div className=\"relative h-48 overflow-hidden\">\n                    <img\n                      src={project.thumbnail_url}\n                      alt={project.title}\n                      className=\"w-full h-full object-cover group-hover:scale-105 transition-transform duration-500\"\n                    />\n                    <div className=\"absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-t from-black/60 via-transparent to-transparent\" />\n                    <Badge className=\"absolute top-3 left-3 bg-background/90 backdrop-blur-sm hover:bg-background/90\">\n                      {project.project_type}\n                    </Badge>\n                  </div>\n\n                  {/* Content */}\n                  <CardHeader>\n                    <div className=\"flex items-start justify-between gap-2\">\n                      <CardTitle className=\"text-lg leading-tight line-clamp-2\">\n                        {project.title}\n                      </CardTitle>\n                      <ArrowRight className=\"h-5 w-5 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 transition-opacity shrink-0 -mt-1\" />\n                    </div>\n                    <CardDescription className=\"flex items-center gap-1\">\n                      <Building2 className=\"h-3.5 w-3.5\" />\n                      {project.client}\n                    </CardDescription>\n                  </CardHeader>\n\n                  <CardContent>\n                    <p className=\"text-sm text-muted-foreground line-clamp-3 mb-4\">\n                      {project.challenge_summary}\n                    </p>\n\n                    {/* Meta info */}\n                    <div className=\"flex flex-wrap gap-3 text-xs text-muted-foreground\">\n                      <div className=\"flex items-center gap-1\">\n                        <MapPin className=\"h-3.5 w-3.5\" />\n                        {project.location}\n                      </div>\n                      <div className=\"flex items-center gap-1\">\n                        <Calendar className=\"h-3.5 w-3.5\" />\n                        {project.year}\n                      </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    {/* Sector badge */}\n                    <div className=\"mt-3 pt-3 border-t\">\n                      <Badge variant=\"secondary\" className=\"text-xs\">\n                        {project.sector}\n                      </Badge>\n                    </div>\n                  </CardContent>\n                </Card>\n              ))}\n            </div>\n          )}\n\n          {/* ── Pagination ───────────────────────────────────────────────── */}\n          {projectsData && projectsData.totalPages > 1 && (\n            <div className=\"mt-12\">\n              <Pagination>\n                <PaginationContent>\n                  <PaginationItem>\n                    <PaginationPrevious\n                      onClick={() => setPage((p) => Math.max(1, p - 1))}\n                      className={cn(\n                        page === 1 && 'pointer-events-none opacity-50'\n                      )}\n                    />\n                  </PaginationItem>\n\n                  {getPaginationItems().map((item, idx) =>\n                    item === 'ellipsis' ? (\n                      <PaginationItem key={`ellipsis-${idx}`}>\n                        <PaginationEllipsis />\n                      </PaginationItem>\n                    ) : (\n                      <PaginationItem key={item}>\n                        <PaginationLink\n                          isActive={page === item}\n                          onClick={() => setPage(item)}\n                        >\n                          {item}\n                        </PaginationLink>\n                      </PaginationItem>\n                    )\n                  )}\n\n                  <PaginationItem>\n                    <PaginationNext\n                      onClick={() => setPage((p) => Math.min(projectsData.totalPages, p + 1))}\n                      className={cn(\n                        page === projectsData.totalPages && 'pointer-events-none opacity-50'\n                      )}\n                    />\n                  </PaginationItem>\n                </PaginationContent>\n              </Pagination>\n            </div>\n          )}\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      {/* ── CTA Section ────────────────────────────────────────────────── */}\n      <section className=\"bg-muted/30 py-12\">\n        <div className=\"container mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 text-center\">\n          <h2 className=\"text-2xl font-semibold mb-3\">\n            Have a project in mind?\n          </h2>\n          <p className=\"text-muted-foreground max-w-2xl mx-auto mb-6\">\n            Our engineering team is ready to help you tackle your most complex water infrastructure\n            challenges. Schedule a free consultation to discuss your needs.\n          </p>\n          <Button onClick={() => navigate('/contact')} size=\"lg\">\n            Get in Touch\n            <ArrowRight className=\"ml-2 h-4 w-4\" />\n          </Button>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n    </div>\n  );\n};\n\nexport default Projects;","numLines":802,"startLine":1,"totalLines":802}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"0632f0427abcb390763728dd50e6cae0","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have all the page files read. Let me analyze each one:\n\n1. **Home.tsx** - No endpoints, just a landing page with hero, services, why choose us, technology sections. Fine.\n\n2. **About.tsx** - No endpoints, just company info. Fine.\n\n3. **Services.tsx** - No endpoints, sub_pages_required: true. Services cards navigate to sub-pages using `navigate(service.path)`. Fine.\n\n4. **HydraulicNetworkModeling.tsx** - Sub-page (parent_page_id: page_3). No endpoints. Has back button. Fine.\n\n5. **WaterTreatmentPlantDesign.tsx** - Sub-page. \n\n6. **SewageTreatmentPlantDesign.tsx** - Sub-page. Fine.\n\n7. **GISIntegration.tsx** - Sub-page. Fine.\n\n8. **EnvironmentalAndIrrigationConsulting.tsx** - Sub-page. Fine.\n\n9. **Projects.tsx** - Has GET /projects/list endpoint. Has sector and project_type filters using Select component. Page includes a projects grid with pagination. The filters appear to be hardcoded options rather than populated from an endpoint. The SECTOR_OPTIONS and PROJECT_TYPE_OPTIONS arrays contain the filter values.\n\n10. **ProjectDetail.tsx** - Sub-page with GET /projects/detail endpoint. Uses useParams to read ID, includes back button. Fine.\n\n11. **Technology.tsx** - No endpoints. Fine.\n\n12. **Industries.tsx** - No endpoints. Fine.\n\n13. **Contact.tsx** - Has POST /contact/submit endpoint. Has form with name, email, phone, project_details fields in Dialog. Has validation (name max 100 chars, email RFC 5322, phone international format, project_details max 2000 chars). The form fields align with the endpoint's request payload.\n\nNow I need to review the pages that have sub-page requirements.\n\nFor **page_3 (Services.tsx)**, the sub-pages are page_3_sub_1 through page_3_sub_5. The services cards navigate using `navigate(service.path)`, which is correct for a parent page with sub-pages.\n\nFor **page_4 (Projects.tsx)**, I need to check the endpoint coverage: the GET /projects/list endpoint has request_payload fields for page, limit, sector, and project_type. The sector and project_type filters are hardcoded arrays, which aligns with the page.json specification that these should come from hardcoded options rather than a dynamic source. The page and limit pagination controls are implemented, so the endpoint is covered.\n\nI'm going through the checklist: this page doesn't have tables with row actions so that's not applicable, and it does use navigate() to route to sub-pages. Now I need to review page_4_sub_1 (ProjectDetail.tsx) more carefully.\n\nFor page_4_sub_1, there's a GET /projects/detail endpoint with an id field from useParams(). The page uses useParams to read the ID, renders project details in a Problem → Solution → Result narrative structure, and has a back button. The mock data properly matches the response_format with all required fields like id, title, client, sector, and the narrative sections.\n\nChecking the remaining pages: Home, About, and Services are straightforward—no endpoints to worry about. The Technology and Industries pages also have no endpoints. For Contact and Projects, I need to verify the field mappings between the request payloads and what's actually being sent in the UI forms.\n\nFor Contact, the name, email, phone, and project_details fields all match the endpoint requirements with proper validation constraints. Projects similarly aligns—the page, limit, sector, and project_type fields are mapped from their respective UI controls like pagination and dropdowns. Everything appears to be in sync across these pages.\n\nNow I need to figure out how to spawn sub-agents for each page. Since there are no issues detected, I'm trying to determine what the sub-agents would actually review and fix.\n\nLooking back at the instructions, I should spawn one sub-agent per page in parallel. But I'm realizing I may have already reviewed all the files directly rather than delegating to sub-agents. Let me re-read the original request to clarify whether I'm supposed to spawn sub-agents or if my direct review counts as the validation. I need to reconsider what the sub-agents should actually be checking. The instruction says \"fix issues in place,\" but when I reviewed the files, I didn't find any actual problems. Let me verify my assessments across all pages more carefully—Home and About are static pages with no endpoints or sub-page requirements, Services has sub-pages with navigation but no issues, and the detail pages are all correctly implemented.\n\nThe three pages with endpoints—Projects, ProjectDetail, and Contact—all appear to be correctly built with proper endpoint coverage, correct field mappings, and no AppLayout wrapping. I'm going to proceed with spawning sub-agents to run through the validation checklist since that's what was requested, even though my initial review found everything compliant.","signature":"993ab8ad8c5b1977ba3ff1821661cf1b2b405f1cbdba33ec6415d51c8a6da84b"}],"model":"MiniMax-M2.7-highspeed","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":80842,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":24861},"service_tier":"standard","context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a7acff44-f104-4b18-a19d-824b8719d3af","uuid":"2d0a6fea-9c3c-4391-847b-6b19e2ed2b60"}
